## Check a real task

1. Identify the exact Home Assistant version, integration, entity capabilities and user permissions.
2. Follow the specification's state matrix and acceptance recipe using synthetic data first.
3. Check keyboard use, narrow layouts, text resizing, reduced motion and the non-visual route. Record the browser and assistive technology actually used.
4. Separate an automated example check from a native task test and a live device observation. Do not report an unrun check as a pass.
5. Keep the native route available when a private host changes or an unsupported capability is encountered.

The [native task accessibility](native-task-accessibility.html) and [compatibility register](compatibility-register.html) pages define these boundaries in detail. The [work-package checklist](../community/guidance-work-package.html) records the implementation and verification evidence for this documentation revision.
